Relevant tables / columns for answering  
• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS  
  – "id": look‑up for Denmark’s boundary relation.  
  – "all_tags": search for `"wikidata" = "Q35"`.  
  – "geometry": multipolygon of Denmark, later converted to GEOGRAPHY for spatial tests.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_WAYS  
  – "geometry": line geometry of every way → highway length.  
  – "all_tags": look for key = "highway" to know the highway class / type.  
  – "id": possible inspection / troubleshooting.  

Optional helper columns  
• "feature_type" (PLANET_FEATURES) – to understand available feature groups, but the main analysis will rely on PLANET_WAYS because highways are line features.  

Typical conditions that will appear in the queries  
1. In PLANET_RELATIONS:  
   LATERAL FLATTEN … WHERE f.value:"key" = 'wikidata' AND f.value:"value" = 'Q35'  
2. In PLANET_WAYS:  
   LATERAL FLATTEN … WHERE f.value:"key"  = 'highway'  
3. Spatial filter:  
   ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(<Denmark_geom>), TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") )  
4. Length computation:  
   ST_LENGTH( TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") ) AS "len_m"  

Below are ten exploratory–to–complete Snowflake SQL statements (all column names are double‑quoted; every query limited to 20 rows for “peek” purposes).

```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at any tags that contain the string 'Q35' in PLANET_RELATIONS
SELECT "id",
       "all_tags"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS"
WHERE  "all_tags" ILIKE '%Q35%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Properly extract the tags for rows whose Wikidata id equals 'Q35'
SELECT r."id",
       f.value:"key"::STRING        AS "key",
       f.value:"value"::STRING      AS "value"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
  AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Get the geometry of the Denmark boundary relation (expect one row)
SELECT "id",
       "geometry"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS"
WHERE  "id" = (
          SELECT r."id"
          FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" r,
                 LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") f
          WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
            AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
          LIMIT 1
       )
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: List a few ways that carry a 'highway' tag (without spatial filter yet)
SELECT w."id",
       w."all_tags"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Show distinct highway types that exist worldwide
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"value"::STRING AS "highway_type"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Bring Denmark geometry into a CTE for re‑use
WITH denmark AS (
    SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom"
    FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" pr,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pr."all_tags") f
    WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
      AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT *
FROM   denmark;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Sample a few highway ways whose geometry is contained in Denmark
WITH denmark AS (
    SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom"
    FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" pr,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pr."all_tags") f
    WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
      AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT w."id",
       ST_LENGTH( TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") ) AS "len_m"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       denmark d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
  AND  ST_INTERSECTS( d."geom", TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") )
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Retrieve highway type and its length for every way inside Denmark
WITH denmark AS (
    SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom"
    FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" pr,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pr."all_tags") f
    WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
      AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT f.value:"value"::STRING                  AS "highway_type",
       ST_LENGTH( TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") ) AS "len_m"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       denmark d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
  AND  ST_INTERSECTS( d."geom", TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") )
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Aggregate total length by highway type inside Denmark
WITH denmark AS (
    SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom"
    FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" pr,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pr."all_tags") f
    WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
      AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT f.value:"value"::STRING                  AS "highway_type",
       SUM( ST_LENGTH( TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") ) ) AS "total_len_m"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       denmark d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
  AND  ST_INTERSECTS( d."geom", TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") )
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY "total_len_m" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final query – five longest highway types in Denmark by summed length
WITH denmark AS (
    SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS "geom"
    FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_RELATIONS" pr,
           LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pr."all_tags") f
    WHERE  f.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
      AND  f.value:"value" = 'Q35'
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT f.value:"value"::STRING                  AS "highway_type",
       SUM( ST_LENGTH( TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") ) ) AS "total_len_m"
FROM   "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_WAYS" w,
       denmark d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w."all_tags") f
WHERE  f.value:"key" = 'highway'
  AND  ST_INTERSECTS( d."geom", TO_GEOGRAPHY(w."geometry") )
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY "total_len_m" DESC
LIMIT  5;
```

The sequence of statements moves from discovering Denmark’s boundary, sampling highway ways, measuring their lengths, to obtaining the top‑5 longest highway categories.
